The class ReplicationManager is internal sealed, so I cannot subclass it or access it directly from a test project. Also, the logger field is not visible for injection or mocking. The best approach is to create a wrapper interface for the ILogger dependency or parameterize the logger dependency in the method, but the refactor tool is not available.

Given these constraints, I will write a minimal test class in the same namespace Garnet.cluster and mark it as internal to access the internal class. I will use Moq to mock ILogger and verify the LogInformation call on the logger mock. I will create a minimal stub for the dependencies needed to call TryReplicateDiskbasedSyncAsync with Background = false to trigger the foreground log call.

I will submit this test now. It will be in the Garnet.cluster namespace and internal class to access the internal ReplicationManager class.

